      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T11:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s not true: Gerrit from v3.9 onwards assures that all `ApiModule` are loaded before all plugins.\n\nPlugins are then loaded into their sandboxed injectors and class loaders and do not see each other.\n\nThe problem here is different IMHO: a Gerrit admin may want to decide, because of its organisation of the rest of the pipeline, the order of generation of events, which is defined by the order of loading of the plugins.\n\nExample: if you load the `pull-replication.jar` and then the `multi-site.jar`, the ref updated event happens *after* the sync replication, therefore the CI/CD would see the change immediately without waits and the reindexing can happen without retries. If you load them in the inverted order, you may end up with failed builds and indexes could take more time to catch-up.\n\nIn the above example, even if the `multi-site.jar` and `pull-replication.jar` do not have direct class dependencies, they still need to be loaded in a very specific order at startup.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90d33b7a_2db371fe",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T11:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That looks like a _hack_ rather than a fix :-)\n`ApiModule` is designed to expose APIs to other plugins and *NOT* to share implementation classes with other plugins.\n\n_[Abu]Using_ the `ApiModule` just for the reason of assuring ordering is wrong.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02c47b11_66483170",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-26T11:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe this _solution_ should be dropped from the commit message, because it is hack that won\u0027t work not even is a short-term solution anyway.\n\nThe current solution to this problem is using symlinks, exactly as Linux [init.d system works](https://www.baeldung.com/linux/systemd-etc-init-d-scripts).\n\nThat is the way the ordering of the plugins is currently achieved, which has one advantage and two main drawbacks:\n\n**Plus**: easy to understand, just list the links in alphabetical order\n\n**Drawbacks**: it\u0027s very manual and prone to errors, also the reloading of the plugins would change the ordering at runtime.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "3e0c45a9df6890d4a2933486c3e4f65aa5777f46",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
